; The SQL bridge: a relational schema read as an olog, and back. It is a
; bridge to a foreign notation, so it lives in tooling/, not core/.
;
; It depends on [writ_data] only: import produces .writ text (so a malformed
; DDL never reaches the engine) and export reads a [Schema.t]. IO-free; the
; `writ sql` verb in tooling/cli/ does the reading and writing.

(library
 (name writ_sql)
 (libraries writ_data))
